---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleHero from '../../components/articles/ArticleHero.astro';
import ArticleContent from '../../components/articles/ArticleContent.astro';
import ArticleStats from '../../components/articles/ArticleStats.astro';
import ArticleContactForm from '../../components/articles/ArticleContactForm.astro';
import ArticleTestimonials from '../../components/articles/ArticleTestimonials.astro';
import ArticleMap from '../../components/articles/ArticleMap.astro';
import ArticleFAQ from '../../components/articles/ArticleFAQ.astro';

const title = "Drunk Driver Accident Lawyer Ann Arbor | Logeman & Iafrate, P.C.";
const description = "Experienced drunk driving accident attorneys in Ann Arbor. We hold negligent drivers and alcohol providers accountable. Free consultation. Call (734) 994-0200.";

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: "What should I do immediately after a drunk driving accident?",
    answer: "First, seek medical attention for any injuries. Call the police to file a report and document the scene with photos if possible. Collect contact information from witnesses and the other driver. Contact an experienced drunk driving accident attorney as soon as possible to protect your rights and begin the investigation process."
  },
  {
    question: "How long do I have to file a drunk driving accident claim in Michigan?",
    answer: "In Michigan, the statute of limitations for personal injury claims is generally three years from the date of the accident. However, for dram shop claims against alcohol providers, you must notify them within 120 days of retaining an attorney. It's crucial to contact a lawyer immediately to ensure all deadlines are met."
  },
  {
    question: "What is a dram shop claim?",
    answer: "A dram shop claim is a legal action against a bar, restaurant, or other establishment that served alcohol to a visibly intoxicated person who then caused an accident. Michigan's dram shop laws allow victims to pursue compensation from these businesses in addition to the drunk driver. These cases require proving the driver was visibly intoxicated when served their last drink."
  },
  {
    question: "What types of compensation can I recover in a drunk driving accident case?",
    answer: "Victims may recover compensation for medical expenses, lost wages, future medical care, pain and suffering, emotional distress, property damage, and in cases of fatality, wrongful death damages. Compensation may come from the at-fault driver's insurance, your own uninsured/underinsured motorist coverage, health insurance, and potentially from dram shop claims."
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need a lawyer for a drunk driving accident claim?",
    answer: "While not legally required, having an experienced attorney is highly recommended. Drunk driving cases involve complex legal issues, multiple potential defendants, strict deadlines, and insurance companies that may try to minimize your compensation. An attorney can thoroughly investigate your case, preserve critical evidence, identify all liable parties, and fight for the full compensation you deserve."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <ArticleHero />
  <ArticleContent>
    <h2>Seeking Justice For Drunk Driving Victims In Ann Arbor</h2>

    <p>Drunk driving accidents shatter lives, leaving a trail of devastation for victims and their families. In Ann Arbor, where safety and community are paramount, the impact of such reckless behavior resonates deeply. At Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., we stand firm against drunk driving and are dedicated to supporting victims in their quest for justice.</p>

    <p>Our experienced legal team understands the complexities and emotional challenges that arise from accidents caused by impaired drivers. We fight tirelessly to hold negligent parties accountable and ensure that victims receive the compensation they deserve for their injuries, pain and suffering. If you or a loved one has been affected by a drunk driving accident, you can trust us to navigate the legal landscape and advocate passionately on your behalf.</p>

    <h2>Potential Liability Of Alcohol Providers: Michigan's Dram Shop Laws</h2>

    <p>In cases where alcohol was served, Michigan's dram shop laws come into play. These laws allow us to pursue claims against businesses like bars, clubs or restaurants that served alcohol to the visibly intoxicated individual who caused the accident. Proving such cases requires showing that the driver was visibly intoxicated when served their last drink. These are intricate cases that demand prompt and thorough investigation to preserve evidence and identify witnesses.</p>

    <h2>Comprehensive Legal Support For Victims</h2>

    <p>We will thoroughly investigate your case to determine the liable parties and help you obtain the support you need. Drunk driving accidents inflict devastating impacts on victims and their families through serious physical injuries, mental trauma, financial strain and fatalities. At our Ann Arbor law firm, we are dedicated to supporting those affected by such reckless actions. Our experienced attorneys are here to help you navigate the complex legal landscape and ensure you receive the full compensation you deserve.</p>

    <p>The primary fault in drunk driving accidents lies with the driver whose impaired judgment led to the incident. Establishing their negligence is crucial, and our team is skilled in handling these sensitive cases to hold the responsible driver accountable.</p>

    <p>Victims of drunk driving accidents might be entitled to recover damages from multiple sources:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>The at-fault driver's insurance policy</li>
      <li>Your own auto insurance, which may include uninsured/underinsured motorist coverage</li>
      <li>Health insurance policies</li>
      <li>Potential dram shop claims against entities that served the driver alcohol</li>
    </ul>

    <p>It is essential to explore these options early to ensure comprehensive coverage for your medical expenses, lost wages and other related costs.</p>

    <p>If you have suffered an injury or lost a loved one due to a drunk driving accident, obtaining legal guidance as soon as possible is critical. Early legal intervention allows us to start an immediate investigation, crucial for dram shop claims, where notification to the alcohol provider must be made within 120 days of the attorney's retention.</p>

    <h2>Contact Us for a Free Consultation In Ann Arbor</h2>

    <p>Don't navigate the aftermath of a drunk driving accident alone. <a href="/contact-us/">Contact our office today</a> to schedule a free consultation. During this meeting, we will discuss your case in detail, explain your legal options, and outline the steps we will take to secure the justice and compensation you deserve.</p>

    <p>Feel free to reach out at any time for advice or assistance with your drunk driver accident injury claim by calling <a href="tel:+17349940200"><strong>(734) 994-0200</strong></a> or by filling out our <a href="/contact-us/">online contact form</a>. We are here to help you through this challenging time and ensure you can focus on healing while we handle the legal aspects. Our lawyers have extensive experience with drunk driving accident claims in Ann Arbor, Detroit and throughout Michigan. We are committed to helping you recover full and fair compensation for your economic losses, and pain and suffering.</p>
  </ArticleContent>
  <ArticleFAQ items={faqItems} />
  <ArticleStats />
  <ArticleContactForm />
  <ArticleTestimonials />
  <ArticleMap />
</BaseLayout>